!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT COULD NOT BE SETTLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) THE JOIN TO p.164 IS NOT CHECKED BY ANYTHING HERE.  Line 4's
!     printed "SLC,$" was replaced by a hard origin, so every check
!     below would still pass if the whole page were at the wrong
!     address.  The page's own witness says 220226.00; p.164's deck
!     is what closes it.
!
! (b) "Z UNLDB" RESTS ON INK ALONE.  Nothing in the repository
!     references it and nothing on this page spells it twice, so
!     neither the comment column, the manuals, nor the assembler
!     can test the D or the B.  A later page branching to it would.
!     ("Z REW ST" is in better shape: the volume OCR of a later
!     page -- an INDEX -- carries "220753.40  220226.10 00  B,Z REW
!     ST  -REWIND", whose .10 is a branch's operation bits on
!     220226.00, this page's own line 5.)
!
! (c) THE LX/SX OFFSET ASYMMETRY of lines 9 and 10, above.  SX,0
!     prints 0o01 and LX,0 prints 0o00 for what the value
!     operations would both make 0o01.  Both rows CHECK, so the
!     deck is not wrong; what is unknown is the rule.
!
! (c') LINE 20'S BYTE IS NOT READ, IT IS DEDUCED -- see GLYPHS (2a).
!     Three rows on this page print a 00 byte whose first glyph is
!     as open as line 20's, so nothing about the paper distinguishes
!     C0 from 00 there.  The row passes because strap_asm encodes
!     BZXE as C0, and strap_asm's BZXE encoding is a SHARED
!     assumption with the fourteen landed decks that print it, so
!     "it checks" is not independent of "the assembler is right".
!     What makes it safe is printed p.159 line 6 carrying the same
!     statement and the same printed word, and printed p.124 line 55
!     carrying a 1800-dpi reading of the same byte -- neither of
!     which is this page.  If BZXE's byte is ever found to be 00,
!     fifteen decks move together and this row is one of them.
!
! (d) THE LOCATION ASTERISK on lines 4, 25 and 35.  Ninth entry in
!     the list of things it is not.  No rule proposed.
!
! (e) THE COMMENT ON LINE 20 reads "-IF NOT, FAKE EPGK" at 400 dpi.
!     "EPGK" is the spelling printed p.160's deck also carries for
!     the same idea, so the two agree -- but it is an abbreviation
!     this repository has never expanded, and a reader who knows
!     what the G is should correct it.
!
! (f) EVERY "DR"/"DRZ" CAVEAT IS VACUOUS HERE -- this page has no
!     reservation, no DD, no VF and no XW.  Nor does it jump its
!     counter: lines 4..29 and 35..38 are contiguous half and full
!     words with no hole, so there is no span to declare.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN FORWARD -- a falsifiable prediction for printed p.166
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 38 is a half-word branch at 220245.00, so THE COUNTER LEAVES
! THIS PAGE AT 220245.40.  Four ways to break that:
!
!   1. printed p.166's first LOCATED row should be 220245.40.
!   2. If p.166 opens with a banner, its heading-row LOCATION field
!      is BLANK and that refutes nothing; a NUMBER there other than
!      220245 does refute it.
!   3. If p.166 prints its own "SLC,$", that row's LOCATION is the
!      counter arriving and must read 220245.40.
!   4. THE CARD SERIAL.  Line 38 here is IL000006, so p.166's line
!      1 should be IL000007 unless p.166 opens a new card deck, in
!      which case it is IM000001 (or the next letter in use).  This
!      page shows the IK->IL boundary falling MID-PAGE at line 32,
!      so a deck change at a page boundary is not required and
!      IL000007 is the prediction.
!
! Also for p.166's transcriber, because this page has already paid
! for them: the UNLOAD routine ends at line 38 after only three
! cards, so whatever p.166 opens with is a NEW routine, not a
! continuation -- and if it carries "REW", "UNLOAD" or any other
! I-O FUNCTION pseudo-op, strap_asm will refuse it the way it
! refused line 11 here.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM   ZREWST   220226.00
!SYM   ZCTLRW   220231.00
!SYM   ZCOMRT   220234.40
!SYM   ZTBRW    220243.00
!SYM   ZUNLDB   220244.00
!CHECK 220226.00 | 220243.40 80 | line 5 Z REW ST SIC,Z TB RW+.32 -- a SIC prints the full 24-bit address, so this checks Z TB RW's bit offset as well as its word: a FORWARD reference to line 28 plus 32 bits, internal to this page
!CHECK 220226.40 | 220234.50 00 | line 6 B,Z COM RT -- same card as line 5; bit 18 set is Z COM RT's .40, which is line 17's own label
!CHECK 220227.00 | 000000.64 8B 001000.36 F0 | line 7 CM1111(BU,1),S REW($11) -- low nibble B is index $11; the second group's 001000.36 is the all-ones connective, printed again on line 26 and against line 23's 001000.00
!CHECK 220230.00 | 220231.00 10 | line 9 LX,0,$+1.0 -- $ is 220230.00 so the target is 220231.00, which is line 11's own location: this row checks the deck's own counter across the CNOP
!CHECK 220230.40 | 000004.01 1C | line 10 SX,0,S IO INS($12) -- same card as line 9; S IO INS is 4.0 and the 0o01 offset is the register encoding (2*0+1), the one index row that fits the value-op rule; the byte's low nibble C is index $12, against line 9's bare 10 -- the two halves of one card printing the same operation with and without an index
!CHECK 220231.00 | 000000.00 8E 000136.15 00 | line 11 Z CTL RW -- PRINTED "REW(SEOP),0.0($14)", COMPILED "CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),(8)136." -- REW admitted 2026-11-02 (0o136 Rewind: RefMan p.132 table, C28-6129 Appendix B, and this row), so the PRINTED form now stands, and the .15 checks CTL(SEOP) against plain CTL's .05
!CHECK 220232.00 | 220233.03 01 | line 12 LVI,1,$+1.0 -- the 0o03 is 2*1+1 for register 1; the address 220233.00 is line 14's location, so this checks the counter
!CHECK 220232.40 | 221261.10 00 | line 13 B,M IO REJ -- same card as line 12; bit 18 clear agrees with M IO REJ at 221261.00 as six other decks write it
!CHECK 220233.00 | 221354.40 80 | line 14 SIC,K EOP R -- a SIC, so K EOP R's offset is OBSERVED to all six octal digits (221354.40), not assumed
!CHECK 220233.40 | 221350.50 00 | line 15 B,K SEOP T -- same card as line 14; bit 18 set is K SEOP T's .40
!CHECK 220234.00 | 216242.10 00 | line 16 B,K SUPP -- bit 18 clear agrees with the fifteen decks that write K SUPP at 216242.0
!CHECK 220234.40 | 000000.45 0D | line 17 Z COM RT V-I,2,.32 -- 0o45 is bit 32 plus 2*2+1; byte 0D is the V-I operation, the same byte strap_asm's own comment records for "V-I,$X15,1.0"
!CHECK 220235.00 | 215265.05 30 | line 18 SV,2,S TIC -- same register 2 as line 17 printing the same 0o05 with no bit-32 term, because S TIC is a .00 symbol
!CHECK 220235.40 | 000004.11 04 | line 19 KVI,4,4.0 -- 0o11 is 2*4+1; the bare 4.0 is word 4 bit 0
!CHECK 220236.00 | 220064.32 C0 | line 20 BZXE,K ILEGL -- byte for byte printed p.159 line 6's word, the SAME statement on another page; the C0 is NOT read off this page's ink (see WHAT COULD NOT BE SETTLED (c')) -- the 0o32 is BZXE's operation bits and bit 18 clear agrees with printed p.160 line 8's own label at 220064.00
!CHECK 220236.40 | 221153.57 01 | line 21 LVI,7,Z EVL RW -- 0o57 is bit 32 plus 2*7+1, and comparing it with line 24's 0o17 on the SAME operation and register is what pins Z EVL RW at .40
!CHECK 220237.00 | 000002.57 3C | line 22 SV,7,S EVL MK($12) -- the identical 0o57 on a symbol independently known to be 2.32, which is what makes line 21's reading an observation and not a convention; low nibble C is index $12 against line 18's bare 30, the same operation without an index
!CHECK 220237.40 | 000004.22 8D 001000.00 F0 | line 23 CM0000(BU,1),S CCW.18($13) -- 0o22 = 18 decimal pins the ".18"; low nibble D is index $13; the second group 001000.00 against lines 7 and 26's 001000.36 checks all four connective digits
!CHECK 220240.40 | 220243.17 01 | line 24 LVI,7,Z TB RW -- 0o17 with no bit-32 term; Z TB RW is this page's own line 28, so this row is fully internal
!CHECK 220241.00 | 000002.17 3C | line 25 SV,7,S EVL TB($12) -- S EVL TB is 2.0 against line 22's S EVL MK at 2.32, same register, 0o17 against 0o57, and byte for byte line 22 (this LOCATION carries the third asterisk)
!CHECK 220241.40 | 000000.74 8B 001000.36 F0 | line 26 CM1111,S CTL($11) -- NO data description, so the length comes from S CTL's own SYN(BU,1); 0o74 is bit 60, which is p.99 line 48's 0.60
!CHECK 220242.40 | 221144.50 00 | line 27 B,Z STEVL -- bit 18 set is Z STEVL's .40, byte for byte printed p.160 line 22's word
!CHECK 220243.00 | 220065.50 00 | line 28 Z TB RW B,K K LOC -- bit 18 set is K K LOC's .40, printed p.160 line 11's own label
!CHECK 220243.40 | 220243.50 00 | line 29 B,$ -- a branch to itself; this is the half word lines 5 and 36 overwrite with the caller's IC, which is why the comment reads "-BRANCH BACK TO MOTHER ROUTINE"
!CHECK 220244.00 | 220243.40 80 | line 36 Z UNLDB SIC,Z TB RW+.32 -- byte for byte line 5's card punched a second time in the IL deck; it lands here only because line 35's printed SLC,$ was written as printed and the counter arrived on its own
!CHECK 220244.40 | 220234.50 00 | line 37 B,Z COM RT -- same card as line 36, and byte for byte line 6
!CHECK 220245.00 | 221733.10 00 | line 38 B,K UNLOD -- the page's last row; bit 18 clear agrees with K UNLOD at 221733.00, and the half word leaves the counter at 220245.40 for printed p.166
